Missing: a header restored with an older time keeps its old references

header.h is replaced by an older version, with its older time, as `cp -p`,
`tar` or a checkout can do. Its time is now older than the change time the
server recorded, and removeReferencesOfChangedFiles() (src/rebuild.c) only
sees a change when the content time is newer. So header.h's references are
not removed, and its includers are not out of date. The request CU is parsed
for the cursor anyway (cursor-parse-reuse) and adds f on line 1, but the
declaration on line 2, which the restored file no longer has, stays.

ADR-0032 accepted this, since make has the same deficiency, so it is Missing
rather than Bug. ADR-0036 (backlog change-is-difference) fixes it: a file has
changed when its modification time and size are not the same as when last
seen, whichever way the time moved. No fix within today's "newer" is wanted.

Written on the Mac, session 4839a129, 2026-11-10, so that each fix ADR-0036
claims has a test waiting for it.
